# Dark Mode Technique for Leaflet Tiles

The gist presents a CSS-based approach to automatically apply dark mode styling to map tiles using the `prefers-color-scheme` media query.

## Implementation Method

The technique assigns a `className` attribute to the tile layer and applies CSS filters conditionally:

**CSS approach:**
```css
:root {
    --map-tiles-filter: brightness(0.6) invert(1) contrast(3) 
                        hue-rotate(200deg) saturate(0.3) brightness(0.7);
}

@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .map-tiles {
        filter: var(--map-tiles-filter, none);
    }
}
```

## Filter Components

The filter chain combines multiple transformations:
- `brightness(0.6)` - Initial darkening
- `invert(1)` - Color inversion
- `contrast(3)` - Contrast enhancement
- `hue-rotate(200deg)` - Hue shift toward cooler tones
- `saturate(0.3)` - Desaturation
- `brightness(0.7)` - Final brightness adjustment

## Variants and Limitations

The gist documents the solution was tested primarily with the OpenStreetMap Humanitarian layer. Commenters confirmed functionality with react-leaflet and other frameworks, but no alternative filter combinations for different tile providers are presented. One discussion mentions CPU performance concerns with filter-based approaches, particularly on lower-end devices.

